# Phase 4 — Image Search

## Task 11 — Select Image Search Provider

Choose an image-search/data provider.

Requirements:

- [ ] Image search capability
- [ ] Search by product name
- [ ] Return image URL
- [ ] Return source URL
- [ ] Return candidate title/metadata where available
- [ ] Reasonable API limits
- [ ] Reliable API
- [ ] Understand pricing
- [ ] Understand rate limits
- [ ] Review commercial usage considerations
- [ ] Review provider terms
- [ ] Review image licensing/usage considerations

### Important

Do **not** build the system around:

```text
Google Images → first result → download
```

The system must treat search results as **candidates**, not automatically correct images.

---

# Phase 5 — Image Search Abstraction

## Task 12 — Create `ImageSearchService`

Create interface:

```typescript
interface ImageSearchService {
  search(query: string): Promise<ImageCandidate[]>;
}
```

Define:

```typescript
type ImageCandidate = {
  imageUrl: string;
  sourceUrl: string;
  title?: string;
  width?: number;
  height?: number;
};
```

- [ ] Define `ImageCandidate`
- [ ] Define `ImageSearchService`
- [ ] Implement provider-specific service
- [ ] Keep provider implementation separate
- [ ] Make provider replaceable

Expected architecture:

```text
ImageSearchService
       │
       ├── Provider A
       │
       ├── Provider B
       │
       └── Future Provider
```

